From 8f3c999127eb6d4bddce9a4a04412dc7f20329f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khaled <khaledchoucri@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:49:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 57/59] POC-17b: Pokemon move with their own Emerald
 animations; big moves get a moment

- Emerald's per-species front animations (sMonFrontAnimIdsTable, pokemon_animation.c) run on
  a puppet sprite the grid owns; its x2/y2, affine matrix (gOamMatrices) and palette glow drive
  our drawing (Gfx_DrawAffine). They play when a Pokemon comes out, and at double speed through
  every wind-up and strike, then ease back (TUNE). PKBN_NO_MON_ANIMS=1 turns them off.
- MegaChips: a 12-frame dark flash with the user lit and rimmed. PAs and GigaChips: a 28-frame
  cut-in - the stage goes black, lines burst out of the user, it's drawn larger, others go dark,
  then a white flash. The fight waits for it (sB.cinemaT); PKBN_NO_CINEMA=1 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FbWSqvcg6G5Gpw6ynvR5tJ
